<DocsLayout title="GitHub Actions">
  <h1>GitHub Actions</h1>
  <p>Identity is published as a public image at <code>ghcr.io/elloloop/identity</code>. Pulling it from a workflow is straightforward; you don't need credentials for the public tag.</p>

  <h2>Pulling the image</h2>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-yaml">jobs:
  smoke-test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    services:
      entdb:
        image: ghcr.io/elloloop/entdb:latest
        ports: ['50051:50051']

      identity:
        image: ghcr.io/elloloop/identity:0.1.0
        env:
          GATEWAY_ENTDB_ADDRESS: entdb:50051
          GATEWAY_DEFAULT_TENANT_ID: ci-smoke
          GATEWAY_AUTH_ALLOW_LOCAL: "true"
        ports: ['80:80', '9090:9090']

    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - name: Wait for identity health
        run: |
          for i in $(seq 1 30); do
            if curl -fsS http://localhost/health; then exit 0; fi
            sleep 2
          done
          exit 1

      - name: Smoke-test signup
        run: |
          curl -fsS -X POST http://localhost/identity.IdentityService/PasswordSignup \
            -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
            -d '{"email":"ci@example.com","password":"Sup3rStrong!Pass"}'</code></pre>

  <Callout type="info" title="Why no GHCR login?">
    <code>ghcr.io/elloloop/identity</code> tags are published as public, so anonymous <code>docker pull</code> and the GitHub Actions <code>services:</code> block work without a <code>docker/login-action</code> step. Pin to a version tag (<code>0.1.0</code>) rather than <code>latest</code> in CI.
  </Callout>

  <h2>How tags are built</h2>
  <p>The <code>release.yml</code> workflow in this repo builds and pushes on every <code>v*</code> git tag. It produces:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>0.1.0</code> &mdash; full semver</li>
    <li><code>0.1</code> &mdash; major.minor</li>
    <li><code>0</code> &mdash; major</li>
    <li><code>latest</code> &mdash; only when the tag is not a prerelease</li>
    <li><code>sha-&lt;commit&gt;</code> &mdash; per-commit pin</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The image is multi-arch (linux/amd64, linux/arm64) and ships with SBOM and provenance attestations.</p>

  <h2>Cutting a release</h2>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-bash">git tag v0.1.0
git push origin v0.1.0
# Workflow runs; image appears at ghcr.io/elloloop/identity:0.1.0</code></pre>

  <h2>Pinning by digest</h2>
  <p>For supply-chain integrity in production, pin by digest rather than tag:</p>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-bash">crane digest ghcr.io/elloloop/identity:0.1.0
# sha256:abcd...

docker run ghcr.io/elloloop/identity@sha256:abcd...</code></pre>

  <h2>Verifying provenance</h2>
  <p>The release workflow attaches a SLSA-style provenance attestation. Verify with <code>cosign</code> or <code>gh attestation verify</code>:</p>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-bash">gh attestation verify \
  oci://ghcr.io/elloloop/identity:0.1.0 \
  --owner elloloop</code></pre>
</DocsLayout>
